WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610
Switch on a kettle, and the metal
element inside it gets very hot.

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.510
Yet the cable that feeds it stays cool.

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.370
Every charge that passes through the
element has come along the cable:

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.610
the same current flows in both.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.880
So why does one get so hot, while
the other hardly warms at all?

6
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.930
In this mission, you'll build
electrical power from two ideas:

7
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.290
joules per coulomb, and
coulombs per second.

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.930
Then you'll work out the energy
a heater transfers on 12 volts,

9
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.720
taking 3 amps for 5 minutes.

10
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:36.990
Your mission: explain why the element
gets very hot while the cable stays cool.
